# fx/arc: A3's Steel Arc: three tones, from a 1 px wisp to 6 px at the blade (behind the body facing right, in front facing down)
# (FX wave 2 r1) R / L a1 re-cut again: the wisp no longer drops behind the head (it began 9 px behind the pivot, outside
# the figure's box); it starts at the crown's front, a row lower (its top row stood over a helmed guard's frame top),
# and the blade end keeps A3's 4 px.
# (FX wave 2 r3) the freeze: the re-cut R / L a1 and the re-cut spark are `when tier1 replace` (the production ladder's
# looks); every P2b look, the hero, heroine and e6m keep e25ea41's views exactly (freeze 0 on P2b from fx).
# (LADDER-ARMS i1) a1 re-cut smaller (the owner, 2026-10-23: oversized, dropping below the feet facing D): 4 px at the
# blade tapering to a 1 px wisp, inside the figure's box plus the blade's reach, its lowest row a pixel above the soles.
# The slice (P2b wave 1, FOLK-BODY); A3's pixels are the reference (docs/ref/style_a3). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body adult
role fx arc
layer fx
anchor pivot
keys fx
legend S fx 3
legend T fx 4

view D key a1 origin 11 14
|C.......................
|C.......................
|C.......................
|CC..................C...
|.C..................CBAA
|.BBC...............BBAAA
|..BBC............CCBAAA.
|....BBCCC...CCCCCBBAA...
|.....BBBCCCCBBBBBAAA....
|........BBBBAAAAA.......

# (LADDER-ARMS polish i1) armed and shielded fighters: the strike's arc a crescent from the shoulder down to the fist,
# its lowest row at the thigh (y -7; the owner: the D swoosh dipped to the shins); the follow's arc (a2) flattened under
# the levelled blade, lowest row at the knee (y -6). The hero keeps A3's arcs (B1 parity).
